// expect-error: T210
// Z3 corpus #26: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 1 refinement violation at construction.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// The rejecting counterpart of fixture #25. The predicate
// `where value > 100` declares a strict lower bound; the construction
// supplies `value: 42`. Z3 returns `Sat` for `not(42 > 100)` (the
// counterexample is the supplied value itself), so T210 fires at the
// construction site.
//
// Per V11, the dispatch maps Z3's `Sat` outcome to a T210 with the
// counterexample. The diagnostic carries (per V7) five fields:
// predicate text, field name, supplied literal, Z3 verdict, source
// span — enforced by the diagnostic-shape test in
// `tests/diagnostic_messages.rs`.
//
// Positive-literal comparison chosen to avoid SIGIL's binary-subtraction
// shape (`0 - 1`) which would be a `TypedExprKind::Binary` and fail V1's
// literal-only check with T211 rather than the intended T210.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
// Same as fixture #25 — this is the negative-evidence half of the pair.
// The verifier MUST reject; fixture #25 MUST accept.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Changing `42` to `101` (or any literal `> 100`) flips this fixture to
// the expect-ok side and would drop T210. Removing `where value > 100;`
// weakens the contract entirely and drops T210.
module sigil;

record Index { value: i64 } where value > 100

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let idx: Index = Index { value: 42 };  // MUTATION_SITE
        return 1;
    }
}
